{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfvVPz6QmHTibHFTi5L6b","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Rivers begin as small streams high in the hills, fed by rain, snowmelt, and underground springs that gather into a steady flow. As they travel downhill, they carve valleys and canyons, slowly reshaping the land over thousands of years. Along their banks, fertile soil and fresh water have supported farms, cities, and entire civilizations since the earliest days of human history. Many rivers also shelter rich ecosystems, from migrating salmon to herons stalking the shallows at dawn. Eventually, nearly every river slows and widens as it reaches the sea, where it releases its water and the sediment it has carried for hundreds of miles."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1489,"cache_read_input_tokens":535,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1489},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000000","uuid":"00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001","timestamp":"2026-10-11T12:59:20.108Z","request_id":"req_REDACTED"}
